Decide every finding. For each, fetch and read the source the finding rests on before deciding; checkers make errors too, so a finding is not true because a checker made it. A proposed new work is adopted only if you located it and it meets the protocol's criteria; the included set stays within 60 works and balanced across the sub-questions, so say which work, if any, it displaces. Record the evidence you saw and its read level. Escalate checker disagreements, conclusion changes and unresolvable gates with two to four options.

Evidence rules (all on):
- EV-3: no claim that a work does not contain, report or compare something may rest on an abstract or record read.
- EV-4: "none", "few", "thin" or "no study" claims about a field are scoped to the searched pool, for example "none of the 54 works screened".
- EV-6: a source read only at record level carries no findings in the output.
